{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-P}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-localize-N}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Japanese-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c0956b48b619a8e78999d2637ac9d13301f638a4ecf0d60cc803a0c4702e0df2", "source_text": "This follows from Lemma <REF_0001> and\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e7ee4196abfbeb360bd2c2508864a02c8aa960314cb8ae855a3df580b5f7c291", "unit_id": "tag:033V:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-universally-Japanese}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8db93e3aab6b3934e5a454525c8915c689822e96fa42d1ba465f98867ae5b80d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is universally Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis universally Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005>\nsuch that each <MATH_0006> is universally Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is universally Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is universally Japanese then every open subscheme\nis universally Japanese.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c00a0b997fdbecb0b6ee87229bba8cfebef151f01dc259ad26acc3436ab94d1f", "unit_id": "tag:033W:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-P}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-universally-japanese}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-nagata-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a901f3558d5ed386b9c08d62fbb6193d894e97450adb7e9653a4133f1ed3b357", "source_text": "This follows from Lemma <REF_0001> and\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e7ee4196abfbeb360bd2c2508864a02c8aa960314cb8ae855a3df580b5f7c291", "unit_id": "tag:033W:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-nagata}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c97fc7fe0fdf83481d0d09dc1ae9f16600af561dfe3449779ddeec874d1c0b3b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is Nagata.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis Nagata.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005>\nsuch that each <MATH_0006> is Nagata.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is Nagata.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is Nagata then every open subscheme is Nagata.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f907bda7c8cb2a38b3a7e172d6312cd84240f8b71357772b7f29582ef9691931", "unit_id": "tag:033X:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-P}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-nagata-localize}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-nagata-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:937962332d47ce4b48fcb2d3e8936ecef00c40039eacb6b159b6569f8e97b8a7", "source_text": "This follows from Lemma <REF_0001> and\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e7ee4196abfbeb360bd2c2508864a02c8aa960314cb8ae855a3df580b5f7c291", "unit_id": "tag:033X:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Z \\subset X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-nagata}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bdf1e6314acb2601fc703166bb56d1e249e72a94c644e1f0cde88e4820e68757", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b65a7c845d6fea67f956fc9d6171685b4d4816870747aeacd14881428445ef37", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme.\nThen <MATH_0002> is Nagata if and only if every integral closed subscheme\n<MATH_0003> is Japanese.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9d426f7536d3b6515a77aa6cf1db0038dd0e0f06fd19f2271e74a46ed9725ea9", "unit_id": "tag:033Y:statement"}
